IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wcra-core`
IMPORT `wcra-seat`

-- Cases for the injured worker's seat (wcra-seat.l4) and the regulative rules of the core (wcra-core.l4).
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited Act (act-2003-027.txt), Regulation (sl-2025-0116.txt) and
-- QOTE Notice (sl-2026-0044.txt), never copied from the encoding's output; the arithmetic is in the comment above each.
-- No scenario life raised this Act and Queensland keeps no requirement ledger: the people are the encoder's,
-- HYPOTHETICAL throughout. Commonwealth figures (the single pension rate, the carer pension rate, a pension
-- income-free amount) and public-holiday counts are HYPOTHETICAL inputs.
--
-- Calendar used (worked by hand from 1 July 2026, a Wednesday): 1 September 2026 is a Tuesday, 1 October a Thursday,
-- 1 November a Sunday, 1 February 2027 a Monday. Monday 5 October 2026 is treated as a Queensland public holiday where
-- a case says "1 public holiday" (HYPOTHETICAL count, as the person would state it).
--
-- A breached or still-pending DEONTIC cannot be asserted on the stable l4, so regulative rules are asserted where the
-- trace ends FULFILLED, and #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line where it does not. A business-day deadline of N "has
-- passed" at the end of day N, written WAITUNTIL N.5 so that the rule that follows starts then.

`2 Sep 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 2 9 2026
`3 Sep 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 3 9 2026
`7 Sep 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 7 9 2026
`9 Sep 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 9 9 2026
`1 Oct 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2026
`3 Aug 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 3 8 2026
`4 Aug 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 4 8 2026
`2 Nov 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 2 11 2026
`19 Oct 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 19 10 2026
`1 Feb 2027`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2027
`2 Mar 2027`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2027
`3 Mar 2027`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 3 3 2027
`25 Mar 2027` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 25 3 2027
`1 Jul 2027`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2027
`15 Jan 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 15 1 2026

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CORE CHECKS: QOTE, s 205, the dates helpers, and the Regulation s 117 example.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Notice s 3(1): $1,994.50 for 2026-27, for any day from 1 July 2026 to 30 June 2027.
#ASSERT `the QOTE for the financial year containing` `2 Sep 2026` `given` 0 EQUALS JUST 1994.50
#ASSERT `the QOTE for the financial year containing` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2027) `given` 0 EQUALS JUST 1994.50
-- After 30 June 2027 no notice is deposited; before 1 July 2026 only the caller's figure.
#ASSERT `the QOTE for the financial year containing` `1 Jul 2027` `given` 2100 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the QOTE for the financial year containing` `15 Jan 2026` `given` 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the QOTE for the financial year containing` `15 Jan 2026` `given` 1953.70 EQUALS JUST 1953.70
-- s 10A(1)(b): a Statistician's figure below last year's QOTE leaves QOTE unchanged.
#ASSERT `QOTE under s 10A(1)` 1980 1994.50 EQUALS 1994.50
#ASSERT `QOTE under s 10A(1)` 2040 1994.50 EQUALS 2040
-- s 205: HYPOTHETICAL QOTE rising from 1,000 to 1,021: $6,298 x 1.021 = $6,430.258, rounded up to $6,435.
#ASSERT `the amount varied under s 205` 6298 `from` 1000 `to` 1021 EQUALS 6435
#ASSERT `the amount varied under s 205` 10000 `from` 1000 `to` 1021 EQUALS 10210
-- s 140 with s 205(2) (finding 4): 216.15 x 1,994.50 = 431,111.175, rounded up to the nearest $5 = 431,115.
#ASSERT `the maximum statutory compensation at` 1994.50 EQUALS 431115
-- Regulation s 117 example: "The maximum statutory compensation is $422,295. The lump sum compensation is $42,229.50."
#ASSERT `the Regulation s 117 product of` 422295 `and a DPI of` 10 EQUALS 42229.50
-- 216.15 x 1,953.70 = 422,292.255, which rounds up to the example's $422,295 (finding 4: a QOTE of $1,953.70 is
-- HYPOTHETICAL, inferred from the example; QOTE for 2025-26 is not deposited).
#ASSERT `the maximum statutory compensation at` 1953.70 EQUALS 422295
-- Regulation s 15: the excess period amount is the lesser of QOTE and the weekly payment: min(1,994.50, 1,232.50).
#ASSERT `the excess period amount under Regulation s 15` 1994.50 1232.50 EQUALS 1232.50
-- Days: 2 Sep 2026 to 2 Mar 2027 is 28 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 31 + 28 + 2 = 181 days; to 2 Sep 2027, 365.
#ASSERT `the days from` `2 Sep 2026` `to` `2 Mar 2027` EQUALS 181
#ASSERT `the days from` `2 Sep 2026` `to` (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 9 2027) EQUALS 365
-- Weekdays: 9 Sep 2026 is a Wednesday; 5 Sep 2026 a Saturday.
#ASSERT `is a Monday to Friday` `9 Sep 2026`
#ASSERT NOT (`is a Monday to Friday` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 9 2026))
-- Monday-to-Friday days after 2 Sep up to 9 Sep 2026: Thu 3, Fri 4, Mon 7, Tue 8, Wed 9 = 5.
#ASSERT `the Monday-to-Friday days after` `2 Sep 2026` `up to` `9 Sep 2026` EQUALS 5
-- Leap years: 2028 is, 2100 is not, 2000 is.
#ASSERT `is a leap year` 2028
#ASSERT NOT (`is a leap year` 2100)
#ASSERT `is a leap year` 2000

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 1. Mia, 34, a warehouse storeperson employed under an award, PAYG employee, insured with WorkCover. On
-- Wednesday 2 September 2026 she hurts her back lifting stock at the warehouse. A doctor sees her that day and
-- certifies her unfit for work; she stops work that day and lodges on Wednesday 9 September 2026. HYPOTHETICAL.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- s 11(1)(a): works under a contract and is a PAYG employee.
#ASSERT `Am I a worker under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE `an ordinary engagement` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a worker under s 11(1)(a): works under a contract and is an employee for PAYG withholding`
-- s 30(1): the person who engages her.
#ASSERT `Who is my employer for workers' compensation` TRUE TRUE FALSE `an ordinary engagement` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the person who engages the worker to perform work (s 30(1))`
-- s 109(2): her employer is not a self-insurer.
#ASSERT `Who must pay my compensation` FALSE EQUALS `WorkCover Queensland (s 109(2))`
#ASSERT `Who must pay my compensation` TRUE EQUALS `the employer, as a self-insurer (s 109(1))`
-- s 32(1), s 34(1)(a): at the warehouse, lifting stock, attended as required, employment a significant contributing
-- factor.
#ASSERT `Is my injury one the Act compensates` `at the place of employment, engaged in an activity for the employer's trade or business` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `an injury (s 32(1)): it arose out of, or in the course of, employment, and employment is a significant contributing factor`
-- The same, with employment NOT a significant contributing factor (a back condition the insurer finds unrelated):
-- s 34(1)(a) deems the course of employment, but s 32(1) still needs the significant contributing factor (finding 5).
#ASSERT `Is my injury one the Act compensates` `at the place of employment, engaged in an activity for the employer's trade or business` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not an injury (s 32(1)): employment is not a significant contributing factor`

-- s 131(1), s 141(1): the entitlement arises on 2 Sep 2026; 6 months after is 2 Mar 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I lodge my application` `2 Sep 2026` EQUALS `2 Mar 2027`
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `2 Sep 2026` `9 Sep 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `in time: lodged within 6 months (s 131(1))`
-- Lodged on the last day, 2 Mar 2027: in time. A day later: late, and no waiver ground: not valid.
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `2 Sep 2026` `2 Mar 2027` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `in time: lodged within 6 months (s 131(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `2 Sep 2026` `3 Mar 2027` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `late: the application is not valid and enforceable (s 131(1))`
-- s 131(4): a tribunal found special medical circumstances: the insurer must waive. (5): lodged within 20 business
-- days of the first assessment of incapacity: may waive. (6): mistake, absence or reasonable cause: may waive.
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `2 Sep 2026` `3 Mar 2027` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `late, but the insurer must waive the limit (s 131(4))`
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `2 Sep 2026` `3 Mar 2027` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `late, but the insurer may waive the limit (s 131(5))`
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `2 Sep 2026` `3 Mar 2027` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `late, but the insurer may waive the limit (s 131(6))`
-- READING at the month end: an entitlement arising on 31 August 2026 must be claimed by 28 February 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I lodge my application` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2026) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2027

-- s 141(2)(a): incapacity assessed on the day she stopped work, so weekly compensation from the next day, 3 Sep 2026;
-- s 131(2) does not bite: 5 business days from 2 to 9 Sep (not more than 20).
#ASSERT `From what day will I be paid weekly compensation` `2 Sep 2026` `9 Sep 2026` `2 Sep 2026` `2 Sep 2026` 0 FALSE EQUALS `3 Sep 2026`
-- s 141(2)(b): if the doctor had first certified incapacity on Monday 7 Sep, weekly compensation from 7 Sep.
#ASSERT `From what day will I be paid weekly compensation` `2 Sep 2026` `9 Sep 2026` `2 Sep 2026` `7 Sep 2026` 0 FALSE EQUALS `7 Sep 2026`

-- s 134(2): 20 business days after Wed 9 Sep 2026, with Mon 5 Oct a public holiday: Thu 10 (1), Fri 11 (2), 14-18
-- (3-7), 21-25 (8-12), 28-30 (13-15), Thu 1 Oct (16), Fri 2 (17), [Mon 5 holiday], Tue 6 (18), Wed 7 (19), Thu 8 (20).
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer decide my application` `9 Sep 2026` 1 EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 8 10 2026
-- Without the holiday: Mon 5 (18), Tue 6 (19), Wed 7 Oct (20).
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer decide my application` `9 Sep 2026` 0 EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 7 10 2026
-- s 134(6): 5 more business days after Thu 8 Oct: Fri 9, Mon 12, Tue 13, Wed 14, Thu 15 Oct 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer tell me why it has not decided` `9 Sep 2026` 1 EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 15 10 2026

-- s 132 with Regulation s 110: the approved form, a doctor's certificate and the evidence: complete. Without the
-- certificate: not.
#ASSERT `Is my application complete` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my application complete` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- s 106, Regulation s 106: 52 weeks; $70,200 base plus $5,200 regular overtime: 75,400 / 52 = 1,450.
#ASSERT `What are my normal weekly earnings` 52 70200 5200 TRUE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS 1450
-- Overtime not regular (Regulation s 106(1)(a)): 70,200 / 52 = 1,350.
#ASSERT `What are my normal weekly earnings` 52 70200 5200 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS 1350
-- s 106(2): employed 26 weeks for $39,000: 39,000 / 26 = 1,500.
#ASSERT `What are my normal weekly earnings` 26 39000 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS 1500
-- Regulation s 108: a second concurrent employer paid $10,400: (52,000 + 10,400) / 52 = 1,200.
#ASSERT `What are my normal weekly earnings` 52 52000 0 FALSE 10400 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS 1200
-- Regulation s 107 (impracticable: a comparable worker's NWE of $1,300) and s 109 (the insurer's fair $1,350).
#ASSERT `What are my normal weekly earnings` 4 6000 0 FALSE 0 TRUE 1300 FALSE 0 EQUALS 1300
#ASSERT `What are my normal weekly earnings` 52 70200 5200 TRUE 0 FALSE 0 TRUE 1350 EQUALS 1350

-- s 150(1)(a), week 1 (September 2026, QOTE 1,994.50): the greater of 85% of 1,450 = 1,232.50 and the award amount
-- 1,180: 1,232.50. s 147: not more than the 1,450 she would have earned.
#ASSERT `How much will I get for a week I cannot work at all` `3 Sep 2026` 0 `employment governed by an industrial instrument (s 150)` 1450 1180 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 575 1 1450 0 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 1232.50
-- Week 30 (March 2027): s 150(1)(b), the greater of 75% of 1,450 = 1,087.50 and 70% of QOTE = 1,396.15: 1,396.15;
-- but s 150(2) caps it at the (1)(a) amount, 1,232.50 (finding 5).
#ASSERT `How much will I get for a week I cannot work at all` `25 Mar 2027` 0 `employment governed by an industrial instrument (s 150)` 1450 1180 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 575 30 1450 0 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 1232.50
-- s 148: the insurer deducts $200 a week for another benefit: 1,232.50 - 200 = 1,032.50.
#ASSERT `How much will I get for a week I cannot work at all` `3 Sep 2026` 0 `employment governed by an industrial instrument (s 150)` 1450 1180 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 575 1 1450 200 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 1032.50
-- s 147: if that week she would have earned only $1,100 at work, she gets 1,100.
#ASSERT `How much will I get for a week I cannot work at all` `3 Sep 2026` 0 `employment governed by an industrial instrument (s 150)` 1450 1180 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 575 1 1100 0 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 1100
-- Week 120, asked on 1 July 2027: no deposited QOTE for 2027-28.
#ASSERT `How much will I get for a week I cannot work at all` `1 Jul 2027` 0 `employment governed by an industrial instrument (s 150)` 1450 1180 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 575 120 1450 0 EQUALS `not covered: no deposited QOTE for that financial year (only 2026-27 is deposited)`

-- s 163 (partial incapacity), week 5: MC is the total incapacity amount, 1,232.50; the s 163(2) formula is missing
-- from the deposit (finding 1), so only the cap is given.
#ASSERT `How much will I get for a week I can partly work` `1 Oct 2026` 0 `employment governed by an industrial instrument (s 150)` 1450 1180 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 575 5 1450 EQUALS `at most this amount a week, in dollars (s 163(3)); the s 163(2) formula is missing from the deposited text` 1232.50
-- s 162: LE = NWE 1,450 - $600 now earned = 850; earning more than NWE gives no loss.
#ASSERT `What is my loss of earnings while I can partly work` 1450 600 EQUALS 850
#ASSERT `What is my loss of earnings while I can partly work` 1450 1500 EQUALS 0

-- s 146B(4)(a): full time: 55% of 1,994.50 = 1,096.975.
#ASSERT `What basic weekly payment will I get while the insurer waits for information` `9 Sep 2026` 0 TRUE 0 38 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 1096.975

-- s 136: back at work on Monday 1 Feb 2027: 10 business days: Tue 2 (1) ... Fri 5 (4), Mon 8 (5) ... Fri 12 (9),
-- Mon 15 Feb 2027 (10).
#ASSERT `By when must I tell the insurer I have gone back to work` `1 Feb 2027` 0 EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 15 2 2027

-- s 144A, s 140 (QOTE 1,994.50; maximum 431,115): still incapacitated, 100 weeks and $120,000 paid: continue.
#ASSERT `When do my weekly payments stop` `1 Oct 2026` 0 FALSE 100 120000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly payments continue`
-- 260 weeks of payments (5 years of 52 weeks): stopped, and all further compensation (s 144A(2)).
#ASSERT `When do my weekly payments stop` `1 Oct 2026` 0 FALSE 260 300000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly payments and all further compensation have stopped: 5 years of weekly payments (s 144A(1)(b), (2))`
-- $431,115 paid: the maximum. $431,112 is above 216.15 x QOTE unrounded (431,111.175) but below the rounded
-- maximum: payments continue (finding 4).
#ASSERT `When do my weekly payments stop` `1 Oct 2026` 0 FALSE 200 431115 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly payments and all further compensation have stopped: the maximum has been paid (s 144A(1)(c), (2), s 140)`
#ASSERT `When do my weekly payments stop` `1 Oct 2026` 0 FALSE 200 431112 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly payments continue`
-- Incapacity over: s 144A(1)(a).
#ASSERT `When do my weekly payments stop` `1 Oct 2026` 0 TRUE 40 50000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly payments have stopped: the incapacity has stopped (s 144A(1)(a))`
-- s 190: she has a notice of assessment and the decision period has run: compensation other than lump sums ends,
-- whether or not she accepts (finding 11).
#ASSERT `When do my weekly payments stop` `1 Oct 2026` 0 FALSE 40 50000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `compensation other than lump sums has stopped: the decision on the lump sum offer was given, or 20 business days passed (s 190)`
-- s 119(2), s 176, s 173(2).
#ASSERT `When do my weekly payments stop` `1 Oct 2026` 0 FALSE 40 50000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `compensation has ended: damages were settled or judgment given (s 119)`
#ASSERT `When do my weekly payments stop` `1 Oct 2026` 0 FALSE 40 50000 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `compensation has ended: a redemption payment was agreed (s 176)`
#ASSERT `When do my weekly payments stop` `1 Oct 2026` 0 FALSE 40 50000 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `compensation has ended: the worker stopped ordinarily residing in Australia (s 173(2))`
#ASSERT `When do my weekly payments stop` `1 Jul 2027` 0 FALSE 40 50000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: no deposited QOTE for that financial year`

-- s 140: the most for one injury in 2026-27 is 431,115; on 15 Jan 2026 with a HYPOTHETICAL QOTE of 1,953.70, the
-- Regulation's example figure 422,295.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can receive for one injury` `1 Oct 2026` 0 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 431115
#ASSERT `What is the most I can receive for one injury` `15 Jan 2026` 1953.70 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 422295
#ASSERT `What is the most I can receive for one injury` `15 Jan 2026` 0 EQUALS `not covered: no deposited QOTE for that financial year (only 2026-27 is deposited)`

-- s 174: (156 x 70% of 1,994.50) - TWP = 156 x 1,396.15 - TWP = 217,799.40 - 100,000 = 117,799.40.
#ASSERT `What is the most my redemption payment can be` `1 Oct 2026` 0 100000 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 117799.40
-- With $250,000 already paid, nothing is left to redeem.
#ASSERT `What is the most my redemption payment can be` `1 Oct 2026` 0 250000 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
-- ss 171-173.
#ASSERT `Can my weekly payments be redeemed` TRUE 110 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the insurer and the worker may agree a redemption payment (s 171)`
#ASSERT `Can my weekly payments be redeemed` TRUE 50 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the insurer and the worker may agree a redemption payment (s 172)`
#ASSERT `Can my weekly payments be redeemed` TRUE 50 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no redemption is available`
#ASSERT `Can my weekly payments be redeemed` TRUE 110 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no redemption is available`
#ASSERT `Can my weekly payments be redeemed` TRUE 50 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the worker stops being entitled to compensation, with no redemption (s 173(2))`
#ASSERT `Can my weekly payments be redeemed` TRUE 50 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the worker is entitled to a redemption payment in an agreed amount (s 173(3))`

-- s 169: injured at 17, review 13 months on: yes; at 12 months exactly: not "more than 12 months".
#ASSERT `Can a review increase my payments because I was injured under 18` TRUE 13 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Can a review increase my payments because I was injured under 18` TRUE 12 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Can a review increase my payments because I was injured under 18` FALSE 24 EQUALS FALSE
-- s 170: paid 5,000, entitled to 4,200: 800 recoverable; underpaid: nothing.
#ASSERT `How much of an overpayment can the insurer recover from me` 5000 4200 EQUALS 800
#ASSERT `How much of an overpayment can the insurer recover from me` 3000 4000 EQUALS 0

-- s 232B: injured 2 Sep 2026, protected to 2 Sep 2027. Dismissed on 1 Sep 2027 for unfitness: contravenes; on
-- 3 Sep 2027: does not; dismissed for another main reason: does not.
#ASSERT `Until when am I protected from dismissal because of my injury` `2 Sep 2026` EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 2 9 2027
#ASSERT `Would dismissing me break s 232B` `2 Sep 2026` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2027) TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Would dismissing me break s 232B` `2 Sep 2026` (DATE_FROM_DMY 3 9 2027) TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Would dismissing me break s 232B` `2 Sep 2026` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2027) FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Would dismissing me break s 232B` `2 Sep 2026` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2027) TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- READING: injured on 29 February 2028, protected to 28 February 2029.
#ASSERT `Until when am I protected from dismissal because of my injury` (DATE_FROM_DMY 29 2 2028) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2029

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 2. Tom, a salaried engineer not under any industrial instrument (s 151), NWE $2,400, totally incapacitated
-- since September 2024. HYPOTHETICAL single pension rate $575 a week.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Week 10: s 151(1)(a), the greater of 85% of 2,400 = 2,040 and 80% of QOTE = 1,595.60: 2,040 (under NWE).
#ASSERT `How much will I get for a week I cannot work at all` `1 Oct 2026` 0 `employment not governed by an industrial instrument (s 151)` 2400 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 575 10 2400 0 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 2040
-- Week 60: s 151(1)(b), the greater of 75% of 2,400 = 1,800 and 1,396.15: 1,800.
#ASSERT `How much will I get for a week I cannot work at all` `1 Oct 2026` 0 `employment not governed by an industrial instrument (s 151)` 2400 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 575 60 2400 0 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 1800
-- Week 110 (October 2026): s 151(1)(c). Having shown a DPI over 15% could result: 1,800. Otherwise: the single
-- pension rate, 575.
#ASSERT `How much will I get for a week I cannot work at all` `1 Oct 2026` 0 `employment not governed by an industrial instrument (s 151)` 2400 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 TRUE 575 110 2400 0 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 1800
#ASSERT `How much will I get for a week I cannot work at all` `1 Oct 2026` 0 `employment not governed by an industrial instrument (s 151)` 2400 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 575 110 2400 0 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 575
-- Week 261: past the first 5 years: none.
#ASSERT `How much will I get for a week I cannot work at all` `1 Oct 2026` 0 `employment not governed by an industrial instrument (s 151)` 2400 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 TRUE 575 261 2400 0 EQUALS `none: past the first 5 years of the incapacity (ss 150-152, 144A)`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 3. Ana, a casual cleaner not under an industrial instrument, NWE $1,000, works about 19 of 38 hours.
-- HYPOTHETICAL.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Week 1: s 151(1)(a), the greater of 850 and 1,595.60 is 1,595.60; s 151(2) and s 153 cap it at NWE: 1,000, all of
-- her NWE (finding 5).
#ASSERT `How much will I get for a week I cannot work at all` `1 Oct 2026` 0 `employment not governed by an industrial instrument (s 151)` 1000 0 TRUE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 575 1 1000 0 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 1000
-- Week 50: the greater of 750 and 1,396.15, capped at NWE: 1,000.
#ASSERT `How much will I get for a week I cannot work at all` `1 Oct 2026` 0 `employment not governed by an industrial instrument (s 151)` 1000 0 TRUE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 575 50 1000 0 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 1000
-- s 146B(5): not full time, 19 of 38 hours: 1,096.975 x 19 / 38 = 548.4875.
#ASSERT `What basic weekly payment will I get while the insurer waits for information` `1 Oct 2026` 0 FALSE 19 38 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 548.4875

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 4. Ray, 68, on the age pension, working part-time for $400 a week under an award when injured. HYPOTHETICAL:
-- he may earn $300 a week before his pension is reduced.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- s 154: the lesser of 400 and 300: 300.
#ASSERT `How much will I get for a week I cannot work at all` `1 Oct 2026` 0 `employment governed by an industrial instrument (s 150)` 400 450 TRUE TRUE 400 300 FALSE 575 3 400 0 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 300

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 5. Who is a worker, and who is the employer: schedules 2 and 3. HYPOTHETICAL.
-- Argument order: contract, PAYG employee, regulated worker, arrangement, sharefarm machinery, share, own business,
-- sublets, employs a worker, does part personally, driving tuition, worker if paid, covered elsewhere, own
-- corporation or Commonwealth, sportsperson, fishing share, unemployment program, PSB determination.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Sam, a teacher who contracts to build a neighbour's fence (not his own trade), does not sublet, employs no one:
-- schedule 2, part 1, item 3; employer: the person who contracted with him (schedule 3, item 6).
#ASSERT `Am I a worker under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE `work as a contractor` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a worker under schedule 2, part 1` 3
#ASSERT `Who is my employer for workers' compensation` TRUE FALSE FALSE `work as a contractor` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the person who made the contract with the contractor (schedule 3, item 6)`
-- Item 3(b) is disjunctive (finding 2): he sublets but employs no worker: still a worker.
#ASSERT `Am I a worker under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE `work as a contractor` FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a worker under schedule 2, part 1` 3
-- He sublets and employs a worker but does part of the work himself: still a worker (item 3(b)(iii)).
#ASSERT `Am I a worker under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE `work as a contractor` FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a worker under schedule 2, part 1` 3
-- He sublets, employs a worker and does none of the work: not a worker.
#ASSERT `Am I a worker under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE `work as a contractor` FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not a worker: neither s 11(1) nor schedule 2, part 1 applies`
#ASSERT `Who is my employer for workers' compensation` TRUE FALSE FALSE `work as a contractor` FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no employer: the person is not a worker`
-- A fencer contracting in his own regular trade: not a worker.
#ASSERT `Am I a worker under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE `work as a contractor` FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not a worker: neither s 11(1) nor schedule 2, part 1 applies`
-- Sam again, but with a personal services business determination in effect: schedule 2, part 2, item 6.
#ASSERT `Am I a worker under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE `work as a contractor` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not a worker under schedule 2, part 2` 6
-- Lena, a PAYG employee of a labour hire agency placed with a host: a worker under s 11(1)(a); her employer is the
-- agency, not the host (schedule 3, item 2).
#ASSERT `Am I a worker under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE `work arranged by a labour hire agency or group training organisation` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a worker under s 11(1)(a): works under a contract and is an employee for PAYG withholding`
#ASSERT `Who is my employer for workers' compensation` TRUE TRUE FALSE `work arranged by a labour hire agency or group training organisation` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the labour hire agency or group training organisation, not the host (schedule 3, item 2)`
-- Jim, a sharefarmer with no powered machinery of his own and 30% of the proceeds: item 1; employer the farm owner
-- (schedule 3, item 4). With half the proceeds: not a worker (more than 1/3).
#ASSERT `Am I a worker under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE `sharefarming` FALSE 0.3 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a worker under schedule 2, part 1` 1
#ASSERT `Who is my employer for workers' compensation` TRUE FALSE FALSE `sharefarming` FALSE 0.3 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the owner of the farm (schedule 3, item 4)`
#ASSERT `Am I a worker under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE `sharefarming` FALSE 0.5 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not a worker: neither s 11(1) nor schedule 2, part 1 applies`
-- Priya, a director employed by her own company and paid through PAYG: schedule 2, part 2, item 1 overrides
-- s 11(1)(a) ("However", s 11(3)).
#ASSERT `Am I a worker under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE `an ordinary engagement` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not a worker under schedule 2, part 2` 1
-- Dev, a food delivery rider covered by a Fair Work Act chapter 3A minimum standards order, not a PAYG employee: not a
-- worker, because the deposited Regulation prescribes no regulated worker (finding 3).
#ASSERT `Am I a worker under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act` TRUE FALSE TRUE `an ordinary engagement` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not a worker: neither s 11(1) nor schedule 2, part 1 applies`
-- Zoe, an unpaid intern who would be a worker if paid: item 7; employer the business (schedule 3, item 8).
#ASSERT `Am I a worker under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act` FALSE FALSE FALSE `unpaid work for experience or a qualification` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a worker under schedule 2, part 1` 7
#ASSERT `Who is my employer for workers' compensation` FALSE FALSE FALSE `unpaid work for experience or a qualification` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the person conducting the business or undertaking the intern works for (schedule 3, item 8)`
-- Ken, a salesperson paid only by commission, not in his own business: item 2; employer the payer (schedule 3,
-- item 5).
#ASSERT `Am I a worker under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE `work paid entirely or partly by commission` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a worker under schedule 2, part 1` 2
#ASSERT `Who is my employer for workers' compensation` TRUE FALSE FALSE `work paid entirely or partly by commission` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the person by whom the commission is payable (schedule 3, item 5)`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 6. Is it an injury: ss 32-36, 113. HYPOTHETICAL. Argument order: setting, attended that day, abnormal risk in
-- recess, drink or dangerous driving, substantial delay or deviation, delay for work or beyond control, otherwise
-- arose in employment, significant contributing factor, psychiatric, management action, connected with Queensland.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- A lunch-break walk to buy food, no abnormal risk: s 34(1)(c), and s 34(2): employment need not contribute.
#ASSERT `Is my injury one the Act compensates` `temporarily absent from the place of employment during an ordinary recess` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `an injury (s 32(2)): a recess or journey injury, for which employment need not be a contributing factor`
-- The same break spent skydiving (an abnormal risk taken voluntarily): s 34(1)(c) fails and nothing else applies.
#ASSERT `Is my injury one the Act compensates` `temporarily absent from the place of employment during an ordinary recess` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not an injury: it did not arise out of, or in the course of, employment`
-- Driving home from work: s 35(1)(a), s 35(2).
#ASSERT `Is my injury one the Act compensates` `on a journey listed in s 35(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `an injury (s 32(2)): a recess or journey injury, for which employment need not be a contributing factor`
-- Driving home over the limit, the offence the major significant factor: s 36(2)(a).
#ASSERT `Is my injury one the Act compensates` `on a journey listed in s 35(1)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not an injury (s 36(2)): the journey injury is excluded`
-- A two-hour detour to a friend's barbecue (a substantial deviation, for no work reason): s 36(2)(b); a detour to
-- collect parts for the employer: s 36(3)(a), still covered.
#ASSERT `Is my injury one the Act compensates` `on a journey listed in s 35(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not an injury (s 36(2)): the journey injury is excluded`
#ASSERT `Is my injury one the Act compensates` `on a journey listed in s 35(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `an injury (s 32(2)): a recess or journey injury, for which employment need not be a contributing factor`
-- Anxiety from a reasonable performance process reasonably run: s 32(5)(a).
#ASSERT `Is my injury one the Act compensates` `at the place of employment, engaged in an activity for the employer's trade or business` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not an injury (s 32(5)): a psychiatric or psychological disorder from reasonable management action or the claim`
-- Employment not connected with Queensland (s 113).
#ASSERT `Is my injury one the Act compensates` `at the place of employment, engaged in an activity for the employer's trade or business` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not compensable here (s 113): the employment is not connected with Queensland`
-- Hurt at work on a day off (not attending "as required"): s 34 does not deem it, but it otherwise arose in the
-- course of employment (s 33) with employment a significant contributing factor: an injury. Without that: not.
#ASSERT `Is my injury one the Act compensates` `at the place of employment, engaged in an activity for the employer's trade or business` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `an injury (s 32(1)): it arose out of, or in the course of, employment, and employment is a significant contributing factor`
#ASSERT `Is my injury one the Act compensates` `at the place of employment, engaged in an activity for the employer's trade or business` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not an injury: it did not arise out of, or in the course of, employment`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 7. Ben is assessed on Monday 3 August 2026, stops work that day and lodges only on Monday 2 November 2026.
-- HYPOTHETICAL. Monday 5 October 2026 is a public holiday in the 20 business days before he lodges.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- s 131(2): 20 business days before Mon 2 Nov, skipping the holiday: Fri 30 Oct (1) ... Tue 6 Oct (19), [Mon 5
-- holiday], Fri 2 Oct (20). Weekly compensation would otherwise start on 4 Aug (s 141(2)(a)); the insurer is liable
-- only from Fri 2 Oct 2026.
#ASSERT `From what day will I be paid weekly compensation` `3 Aug 2026` `2 Nov 2026` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2026` 1 FALSE EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 2 10 2026
-- If the insurer waives s 131(2) under s 131(6): from 4 Aug 2026.
#ASSERT `From what day will I be paid weekly compensation` `3 Aug 2026` `2 Nov 2026` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2026` 1 TRUE EQUALS `4 Aug 2026`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 8. Permanent impairment. Mia's back is assessed: DPI 10%. The insurer received the assessment on Thursday
-- 1 October 2026 (1 public holiday in the following fortnight) and gave the notice on Monday 19 October 2026.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- s 185: 10 business days after Thu 1 Oct: Fri 2 (1), [Mon 5 holiday], Tue 6 (2) ... Fri 9 (5), Mon 12 (6) ...
-- Fri 16 Oct 2026 (10).
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer give me my notice of assessment` `1 Oct 2026` 1 EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 16 10 2026
-- Regulation s 117: 431,115 x 10% = 43,111.50.
#ASSERT `What lump sum does my DPI give me` `19 Oct 2026` 0 10 0 0 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 43111.50
-- s 180(2): 2% of the 10% is from an earlier condition: 431,115 x 8% = 34,489.20.
#ASSERT `What lump sum does my DPI give me` `19 Oct 2026` 0 10 2 0 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 34489.20
-- s 181: an earlier entitlement of $10,000 for the same part of the body: 43,111.50 - 10,000 = 33,111.50.
#ASSERT `What lump sum does my DPI give me` `19 Oct 2026` 0 10 0 10000 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 33111.50
-- The Regulation s 117 example itself, on 15 Jan 2026 with the HYPOTHETICAL QOTE 1,953.70: 422,295 x 10% =
-- 42,229.50.
#ASSERT `What lump sum does my DPI give me` `15 Jan 2026` 1953.70 10 0 0 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 42229.50
-- s 186(2), ss 188-190: the decision period is 20 business days after Mon 19 Oct: 20-23 (1-4), 26-30 (5-9),
-- 2-6 Nov (10-14), 9-13 (15-19), Mon 16 Nov 2026 (20).
#ASSERT `By when must I tell the insurer I disagree with my DPI` `19 Oct 2026` 0 EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 16 11 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I decide about the lump sum offer` `19 Oct 2026` 0 EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 16 11 2026
-- ss 189, 237(3), 239: under 20%, accepting is the irrevocable election; 20% or more, not; no DPI, still an election.
#ASSERT `What do I give up by accepting the lump sum offer` 10 EQUALS `DPI under 20%: accepting is an irrevocable election not to seek damages; other compensation ends at the decision or after 20 business days (ss 189, 190, 237(3), 239)`
#ASSERT `What do I give up by accepting the lump sum offer` 20 EQUALS `DPI 20% or more: accepting or deferring keeps the right to seek damages; other compensation ends at the decision or after 20 business days (ss 188, 190)`
#ASSERT `What do I give up by accepting the lump sum offer` 0 EQUALS `no DPI: no lump sum is offered; the worker must still elect whether to seek damages (s 189(1)(b), (2))`

-- s 192, schedule 3: DPI 30%: 8.15 x 1,994.50 = 16,255.175, up to $16,260. DPI 45%: 77.48 x 1,994.50 = 154,533.86,
-- up to 154,535. DPI 74%: 211.53 x 1,994.50 = 421,896.585, up to 421,900. DPI 80% (75-100 row): 431,115.
#ASSERT `What additional lump sum do I get for a DPI of 30% or more` `19 Oct 2026` 0 30 FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 16260
#ASSERT `What additional lump sum do I get for a DPI of 30% or more` `19 Oct 2026` 0 45 FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 154535
#ASSERT `What additional lump sum do I get for a DPI of 30% or more` `19 Oct 2026` 0 74 FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 421900
#ASSERT `What additional lump sum do I get for a DPI of 30% or more` `19 Oct 2026` 0 80 FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 431115
-- DPI 29%: none. DPI 50% from a psychiatric injury: none (s 192(3)).
#ASSERT `What additional lump sum do I get for a DPI of 30% or more` `19 Oct 2026` 0 29 FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
#ASSERT `What additional lump sum do I get for a DPI of 30% or more` `19 Oct 2026` 0 50 TRUE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 0

-- s 193, schedule 4: DPI 55%, modified barthel index 30 (severe), cared for at home unpaid, all conditions met:
-- 32.68 x 1,994.50 = 65,180.26, up to 65,185.
#ASSERT `What additional lump sum do I get for gratuitous care` `19 Oct 2026` 0 55 30 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 65185
-- DPI 20%, index 60 (moderate): 1.99 x 1,994.50 = 3,969.055, up to 3,970.
#ASSERT `What additional lump sum do I get for gratuitous care` `19 Oct 2026` 0 20 60 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 3970
-- DPI 96%, index 10 (total): 244.86 x 1,994.50 = 488,373.27, up to 488,375.
#ASSERT `What additional lump sum do I get for gratuitous care` `19 Oct 2026` 0 96 10 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 488375
-- Index 80 (mild, not moderate to total), DPI 14%, care provided before, or a psychiatric DPI: none.
#ASSERT `What additional lump sum do I get for gratuitous care` `19 Oct 2026` 0 55 80 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
#ASSERT `What additional lump sum do I get for gratuitous care` `19 Oct 2026` 0 14 30 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
#ASSERT `What additional lump sum do I get for gratuitous care` `19 Oct 2026` 0 55 30 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
#ASSERT `What additional lump sum do I get for gratuitous care` `19 Oct 2026` 0 55 30 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 0

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 9. Death. Mia asks what her family would get if she died from the injury. HYPOTHETICAL. Argument order: day,
-- earlier QOTE, someone totally dependent, family dependent, spouse totally dependent, members under 6, children
-- under 16 or students, insurer's reasonable amount, spouse/issue/next of kin, terminal latent onset compensated.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- A totally dependent husband and two children, aged 4 and 9. s 200(2)(a): 404.87 x 1,994.50 = 807,513.215, up to
-- 807,515; (aa): 10.83 x 1,994.50 = 21,600.435, up to 21,605; (b): 21.64 x 1,994.50 = 43,160.98, up to 43,165, for
-- each of 2 children = 86,330. Total 807,515 + 21,605 + 86,330 = 915,450.
#ASSERT `What lump sum would be paid for my death` `1 Oct 2026` 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE 1 2 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 915450
-- Weekly: (ab) 8% of QOTE = 159.56 for the spouse while a child is under 6; (c) 10% of QOTE = 199.45 for each of 2
-- children = 398.90. Total 558.46.
#ASSERT `What weekly amounts would be paid for my death` `1 Oct 2026` 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE 1 2 FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 558.46
-- Once the younger child is 6 (no member under 6): weekly 398.90.
#ASSERT `What weekly amounts would be paid for my death` `1 Oct 2026` 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 2 FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 398.90
-- s 201: only partly dependent parents; the insurer thinks $50,000 reasonable: raised to the floor, 15% of 807,515 =
-- 121,127.25. At $200,000: 200,000. At $900,000: capped at 807,515.
#ASSERT `What lump sum would be paid for my death` `1 Oct 2026` 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 0 50000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 121127.25
#ASSERT `What lump sum would be paid for my death` `1 Oct 2026` 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 0 200000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 200000
#ASSERT `What lump sum would be paid for my death` `1 Oct 2026` 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 0 900000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 807515
-- s 201(2)(b): a partly dependent child under 16: 7% of QOTE = 139.615 a week.
#ASSERT `What weekly amounts would be paid for my death` `1 Oct 2026` 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 1 FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 139.615
-- s 201A: no dependants, a non-dependent spouse: 10% of 807,515 = 80,751.50 to the estate.
#ASSERT `What lump sum would be paid for my death` `1 Oct 2026` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 80751.50
-- No dependants and no spouse, issue or next of kin: nothing under ss 200-201A.
#ASSERT `What lump sum would be paid for my death` `1 Oct 2026` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
-- s 194(2): a terminal latent onset injury already compensated: part 11 does not apply.
#ASSERT `What lump sum would be paid for my death` `1 Oct 2026` 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE 1 2 0 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `none: part 11 does not apply to a terminal latent onset injury already compensated (s 194(2))`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 10. Care and rehabilitation. HYPOTHETICAL carer pension rate: $560.00 a week.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Regulation s 147, schedule 8: index 30 (severe): at most 23.5 hours x (560 / 35 = 16) = 376 a week. Index 95
-- (minimal): 10 x 16 = 160. Index 100 (no dependency): 0. Not receiving weekly payments: 0.
#ASSERT `What is the most caring allowance that can be paid each week` TRUE 30 TRUE 560 EQUALS 376
#ASSERT `What is the most caring allowance that can be paid each week` TRUE 95 TRUE 560 EQUALS 160
#ASSERT `What is the most caring allowance that can be paid each week` TRUE 100 TRUE 560 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What is the most caring allowance that can be paid each week` FALSE 30 TRUE 560 EQUALS 0
-- s 220(3)(b): asked to be referred: yes. (3)(c): stopped under s 144A, not back at work, not in a program: yes;
-- already in one: no. (4)(a): the insurer is satisfied a program cannot help: no.
#ASSERT `Must the insurer refer me to a rehabilitation program` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the insurer refer me to a rehabilitation program` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the insurer refer me to a rehabilitation program` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the insurer refer me to a rehabilitation program` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 232(2): refused without excuse: may suspend; with a reasonable excuse: may not.
#ASSERT `Can the insurer suspend my compensation for not taking part in rehabilitation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the insurer suspend my compensation for not taking part in rehabilitation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- REGULATIVE RULES (wcra-core.l4). Day 0 is the day each rule starts; the clock is in the rule's own unit.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- s 131 (calendar days; Mia: 181 days from 2 Sep 2026 to 2 Mar 2027). Lodged on day 7: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 131 -- the claimant must lodge the application within 6 months after the entitlement arises` 181 FALSE FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `lodge the application for compensation` 7)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Lodged on day 181, the last day: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 131 -- the claimant must lodge the application within 6 months after the entitlement arises` 181 FALSE FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `lodge the application for compensation` 181)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Late, with a tribunal's finding of special medical circumstances: the insurer waives: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 131 -- the claimant must lodge the application within 6 months after the entitlement arises` 181 TRUE FALSE) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 182), (EVENT `the insurer` `waive the s 131(1) time limit` 200)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Late, with a s 131(5) or (6) ground, and the insurer waives: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 131 -- the claimant must lodge the application within 6 months after the entitlement arises` 181 FALSE TRUE) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 182), (EVENT `the insurer` `waive the s 131(1) time limit` 190)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the claimant, "s 131(1): an application lodged more than 6 months after ..." (late, no ground)
#TRACE (`s 131 -- the claimant must lodge the application within 6 months after the entitlement arises` 181 FALSE FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 182)
-- expect: the insurer's duty to waive, still pending (late, special medical circumstances, not yet waived)
#TRACE (`s 131 -- the claimant must lodge the application within 6 months after the entitlement arises` 181 TRUE FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 182)

-- s 132AA: both statements given: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 132AA -- the insurer must give the worker and the employer an information statement` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `give the worker the information statement` 2), (EVENT `the insurer` `give the employer the information statement` 3)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the employer's statement still owed, with no time ever passing it (no WITHIN: "as soon as practicable")
#TRACE `s 132AA -- the insurer must give the worker and the employer an information statement` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the insurer` DOES `give the worker the information statement` AT 2
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- s 133 (business days from the employer learning of the injury). Report on day 8: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 133 -- the employer must report the injury to the insurer` FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the employer` `give the insurer the injury report` 8)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- A reasonable excuse, report on day 12: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 133 -- the employer must report the injury to the insurer` TRUE) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 8.5), (EVENT `the employer` `give the insurer the injury report` 12)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the employer, "s 133(3): ... within 8 business days ..." (no report by day 8, no excuse)
#TRACE (`s 133 -- the employer must report the injury to the insurer` FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 8.5)

-- s 134 (business days from the application). Allowed on day 15, notified on day 16: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 134 -- the insurer must decide the application within 20 business days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` (`decide the application` `allowed`) 15), (EVENT `the insurer` `notify the claimant of the decision` 16)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Rejected on day 20 (in time), notified with reasons and the prescribed information on day 21: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 134 -- the insurer must decide the application within 20 business days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` (`decide the application` `rejected`) 20), (EVENT `the insurer` `notify the claimant of the rejection with written reasons and the prescribed information` 21)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- No decision by the end of day 20; the s 134(6) notice on day 25: fulfilled (finding 8: the late decision is the
-- LEST path taken).
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 134 -- the insurer must decide the application within 20 business days` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 20.5), (EVENT `the insurer` `notify the claimant of its reasons for not deciding and of the right to a review` 25)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the insurer, "s 134(2), (6): ..." (no decision by day 20, no notice by day 25; the s 134(6) rule
-- starts at 20.5, so its 5 days run to 25.5 and day 26 is past them)
#TRACE `s 134 -- the insurer must decide the application within 20 business days` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 20.5)
    (WAITUNTIL 26)
-- expect: the duty to give written reasons still pending (rejected in time, told without reasons; s 134(3) sets no time)
#TRACE `s 134 -- the insurer must decide the application within 20 business days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the insurer` DOES `decide the application` `rejected` AT 18
    PARTY `the insurer` DOES `notify the claimant of the decision` AT 19

-- s 136 (business days from the return to work). Notice on day 10: fulfilled. Not receiving compensation: nothing.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 136 -- the worker must notify the insurer of a return to work within 10 business days` TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` `notify the insurer of the return to work or engagement in a calling` 10)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 136 -- the worker must notify the insurer of a return to work within 10 business days` FALSE) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 30)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the worker, "s 136(1): ..." (no notice by day 10)
#TRACE (`s 136 -- the worker must notify the insurer of a return to work within 10 business days` TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10.5)

-- s 144: Mia's award does not pay the day she stopped work; she would have earned $290 that day. Paid $290:
-- fulfilled. If part 8 does not apply: nothing owed.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 144 -- the employer must pay the worker for the day of injury` TRUE 290) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the employer` (`pay the worker for the day of injury` 290) 3)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 144 -- the employer must pay the worker for the day of injury` FALSE 290) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 30)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the employer's duty to pay $290 still pending (it paid $200, which does not count)
#TRACE (`s 144 -- the employer must pay the worker for the day of injury` TRUE 290) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the worker for the day of injury` 200 AT 3

-- s 146B (business days from the decision to allow). The insurer has the information: nothing under s 146B.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 146B -- the insurer must start the basic weekly payment while it waits for information` TRUE 3) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 30)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Without it, excess period ending at business day 3: by day 5 (the later); started on day 5: fulfilled. Excess
-- period ending at day 7: started on day 7: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 146B -- the insurer must start the basic weekly payment while it waits for information` FALSE 3) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `start the basic weekly payment` 5)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 146B -- the insurer must start the basic weekly payment while it waits for information` FALSE 7) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `start the basic weekly payment` 7)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the insurer, "s 146B(3): ..." (started on day 6, the deadline being day 5)
#TRACE (`s 146B -- the insurer must start the basic weekly payment while it waits for information` FALSE 3) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the insurer` DOES `start the basic weekly payment` AT 6

-- s 185 (business days from receipt of the assessment). DPI under 20%: notice and the s 189(2) sections by day 10:
-- fulfilled. DPI 20% or more: the notice alone: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 185 -- the insurer must give the notice of assessment within 10 business days` TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `give the worker the notice of assessment, with any offer` 10), (EVENT `the insurer` `give the worker copies of ss 10, 237(3), 239, 240 and 316 and advise of the irrevocable election` 10)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 185 -- the insurer must give the notice of assessment within 10 business days` FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `give the worker the notice of assessment, with any offer` 9)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the insurer, "s 189(2): ..." (DPI under 20%, the notice without the sections)
#TRACE (`s 185 -- the insurer must give the notice of assessment within 10 business days` TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the insurer` DOES `give the worker the notice of assessment, with any offer` AT 10
    (WAITUNTIL 10.5)

-- s 186 (business days from the notice). Already assessed by a tribunal: no s 186 route. No disagreement within the
-- decision period: the notice stands: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 186 -- disagreeing with the DPI in the notice of assessment` TRUE) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 30)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 186 -- disagreeing with the DPI in the notice of assessment` FALSE) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 20.5)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Disagrees on day 5 and asks for another assessment; the insurer agrees on day 12 (within 10 of day 5): fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 186 -- disagreeing with the DPI in the notice of assessment` FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` (`advise the insurer of disagreement with the DPI` `assess the injury again by a different entity`) 5), (EVENT `the insurer` (`decide whether to have the injury assessed again` TRUE) 12)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- The insurer declines on day 12 and refers the DPI to a tribunal on day 20: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 186 -- disagreeing with the DPI in the notice of assessment` FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` (`advise the insurer of disagreement with the DPI` `assess the injury again by a different entity`) 5), (EVENT `the insurer` (`decide whether to have the injury assessed again` FALSE) 12), (EVENT `the insurer` `refer the DPI to a medical assessment tribunal` 20)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Asks for a tribunal on day 5; the insurer refers on day 9: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 186 -- disagreeing with the DPI in the notice of assessment` FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` (`advise the insurer of disagreement with the DPI` `refer the DPI to a medical assessment tribunal`) 5), (EVENT `the insurer` `refer the DPI to a medical assessment tribunal` 9)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the insurer, "s 186(3): ..." (asked on day 5, no decision by day 15)
#TRACE (`s 186 -- disagreeing with the DPI in the notice of assessment` FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the worker` DOES `advise the insurer of disagreement with the DPI` `assess the injury again by a different entity` AT 5
    (WAITUNTIL 15.5)

-- ss 188, 189 (business days from the notice). DPI 10%: accepts on day 10, the insurer pays 43,111.50: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 188, 189 -- deciding about the lump sum offer within the decision period` 43111.50 FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` (`give the insurer written notice about the offer` `accept the offer`) 10), (EVENT `the insurer` (`pay the lump sum` 43111.50) 15)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- DPI 10%: rejects on day 5 (and will seek damages): fulfilled; defers: fulfilled; silent: taken to defer.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 188, 189 -- deciding about the lump sum offer within the decision period` 43111.50 FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` (`give the insurer written notice about the offer` `reject the offer`) 5)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 188, 189 -- deciding about the lump sum offer within the decision period` 43111.50 FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` (`give the insurer written notice about the offer` `defer the decision`) 5)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 188, 189 -- deciding about the lump sum offer within the decision period` 43111.50 FALSE) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 20.5)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- DPI 25%: a "rejection" is not an answer s 188 allows; it does not count, and silence is a deferral: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 188, 189 -- deciding about the lump sum offer within the decision period` 107778.75 TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` (`give the insurer written notice about the offer` `reject the offer`) 5), (WAITUNTIL 20.5)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the insurer's duty to pay 43,111.50 still pending (accepted on day 10, not paid; no time is stated)
#TRACE (`ss 188, 189 -- deciding about the lump sum offer within the decision period` 43111.50 FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the worker` DOES `give the insurer written notice about the offer` `accept the offer` AT 10
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

-- s 220(3): a referral required, and made: fulfilled; not required: nothing.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 220(3) -- the insurer must refer the worker to an accredited rehabilitation and return to work program` TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `refer the worker to an accredited rehabilitation and return to work program` 4)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 220(3) -- the insurer must refer the worker to an accredited rehabilitation and return to work program` FALSE) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 30)) EQUALS FULFILLED

-- s 232 (calendar days entitled: 90). Participates throughout: fulfilled. Refuses on day 10 and is suspended by
-- notice on day 12: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 232 -- the worker must participate in rehabilitation` 90) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 91)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 232 -- the worker must participate in rehabilitation` 90) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` `fail or refuse to participate in rehabilitation without reasonable excuse` 10), (EVENT `the insurer` `suspend the worker's compensation by written notice` 12)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the insurer's permission to suspend, still open (refused on day 10; suspension is not a breach by the worker)
#TRACE (`s 232 -- the worker must participate in rehabilitation` 90) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the worker` DOES `fail or refuse to participate in rehabilitation without reasonable excuse` AT 10

-- s 232B (calendar days; Mia: 365 from 2 Sep 2026 to 2 Sep 2027). No dismissal within the 12 months: fulfilled; a
-- dismissal on day 366 is after the protection and is not matched: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 232B -- the employer must not dismiss the worker for unfitness because of the injury within 12 months` 365) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 366)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 232B -- the employer must not dismiss the worker for unfitness because of the injury within 12 months` 365) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the employer` `dismiss the worker solely or mainly because the worker is unfit because of the injury` 366)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the employer, "s 232B(1): ..." (dismissed for unfitness on day 200)
#TRACE (`s 232B -- the employer must not dismiss the worker for unfitness because of the injury within 12 months` 365) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `dismiss the worker solely or mainly because the worker is unfit because of the injury` AT 200
